{"id":"{{PREFIX}}-d1","issue_type":"decision","title":"Internal D1: testid contract for the target SPA","description":"# Contract\n\nThe target SPA exposes the following data-testids (consumed by the acceptance oracle and by the agent's vitest specs):\n\n| Surface | testid |\n|---|---|\n| App root wrapper | `app-root` |\n| Conversion table root | `temperature-table` |\n| Per-row | `row-{celsius}` where celsius ∈ {0, 20, 40, ..., 300} |\n\nNo other testids are required. Agents implementing components must use exactly these names — D18 (the acceptance oracle, gm-bvlm) keys assertions on them.\n\n# Why these specifically\n\n- `app-root` is stable across M2 (Hello world) and M3 (table) so the M2 oracle doesn't need to flip when M3 lands.\n- `row-{celsius}` encodes the source-of-truth in the testid itself, so the oracle's row-→-temperature mapping is self-checking.\n","status":"open","priority":2,"labels":["acceptance","d:contract","decision"],"created_at":"2026-04-30T00:00:00Z","updated_at":"2026-04-30T00:00:00Z"}
{"id":"{{PREFIX}}-d2","issue_type":"decision","title":"Internal D2: acceptance-engineer persona — skill set + done flow","description":"# Persona shape\n\nThe pool routes work to the `acceptance-engineer` persona. The persona has the minimum skill set the M1/M2/M3 task templates require:\n\n| Skill | Used by |\n|---|---|\n| Write files | every template |\n| Run `npm install` (with `--offline`) | npm-install template |\n| Run `npm run build` (vite) | build template |\n| Run `npm test` (vitest) | write-test, build templates |\n| Run `vite preview` | serve template |\n\nThe done flow is pinned to the `/done` slash command (per gm-s47n.14) so the post-bead emit of `gemba-state bead-done` reliably triggers SessionReady — pool reuse works across both native and gastown variants today.\n\nDirect `gt done` would not emit until gm-s47n.20 lands; the persona deliberately doesn't use that path.\n","status":"open","priority":2,"labels":["acceptance","d:persona","decision"],"created_at":"2026-04-30T00:00:00Z","updated_at":"2026-04-30T00:00:00Z"}
